{"model_uid": "250dc8f51ee444679ad7ba6c3010c7a7", "comment_uid": "72ec2c2581ff4e6ebcb8a1c530e82069", "username": "Proflibrary09", "displayName": "Proflibrary09", "body": "Has anyone 3D printed this skull version?    💀\n\nI'm new to 3D printing and would love to hear from people who have successfully printed it. The model looks highly detailed, but I'm curious how well those details translate into a physical print.\n\n❓ A few questions:\n\n* Is the model already suitable for 3D printing, or does it require repair or cleanup first?\n* Did you print the entire skeleton/skull as one piece or split it into multiple parts?\n* What scale did you use?\n* Which printer type gave the best results (FDM or resin)?\n* How well are the fine details, such as teeth, sutures, and bone texture, preserved?\n* Were supports needed, and if so, where?\n* Are there any parts that are fragile or difficult to print?\n* What settings would you recommend for someone attempting their first fossil print?\n\nI'd appreciate any tips, photos, or lessons learned. My goal is to produce the most accurate and detailed print possible while preserving the scientific value of the specimen.\n\nThanks for any advice!", "isDeleted": false, "createdAt": "2026-06-04T08:23:40.780261", "updatedAt": "2026-06-04T08:23:40.780278"}
