{"model_uid": "38324e0d3e1c4303aa34941959fee12b", "comment_uid": "96b97b8794f54ae19a26be76f91fff9e", "username": "Shaacofiri", "displayName": "Shaacofiri", "body": "FOR THOSE EXPERIENCING FUR ISSUES\n\nIf your fur looks thick and stiff, try this solution:\n\nTo fix the fur issue in Unreal Engine, go to WolfFurMaterial and then\n\nBlending Mode: Masked\n\nShading Model: Hair\n\nTwo-Sided\n\nCreate Ray-Traced Shadows\n\nand set the Roughness Value to 5.0\n\nSet the Specular Value to 0.2\n\nSet the Diffusion Value to 0.8\n\nAdd the DitherTemporalAA node from the Texture Sample’s RGB section and connect it to the Opacity Mask", "isDeleted": false, "createdAt": "2026-06-04T11:20:24.932315", "updatedAt": "2026-06-04T11:20:24.932329"}
